WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.050
A continent's quiet interior preserves a long history.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.830
A shield exposes old igneous and metamorphic crystalline basement.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:12.870
A platform covers similar basement with younger, mostly horizontal sedimentary layers.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.270
These are different surface expressions, not completely unrelated kinds of deep

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.450
crust. The boundary between basement and cover is a major unconformity,

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.690
recording missing time and an earlier history of formation, uplift, and

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:26.050
erosion.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.880
Across Ohio, Paleozoic layers dip gently away from the Findlay Arch,

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.840
above Precambrian basement encountered in drill holes.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.940
The cross section exaggerates vertical scale, so the real dips are

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.940
gentler than they look. Always read that disclosure before interpreting a

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.900
diagram as a literal landscape.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.080
Small dips over broad distances can expose different layers across a

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:49.720
large region.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.990
Stable does not mean unaffected.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.670
Loads and tectonic stresses along a continental margin can bend the

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.310
interior or reactivate ancient basement faults.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.590
Those movements may produce broad uplifts, basins, folds, and faults in

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.150
the cover. Most interior faults may be inactive, but the setting

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.790
does not rule out active deformation.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.600
Low-relief continents are sensitive to sea level.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.380
A rise of only tens of meters can flood a wide

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.520
area, leaving shallow-marine sediment far inland.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.000
Climate also changes with global conditions, nearby mountain building, and a

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.580
continent's latitude. Flat-lying layers can therefore preserve rivers, lakes, dunes, beaches,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.160
or seas. Horizontal bedding alone does not identify the original environment.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.870
Mountains in a continental interior can mark an old plate boundary.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.270
The Urals formed when landmasses collided and became joined, leaving the

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.130
mountain belt inside the larger continent.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.670
Today's geography is only the latest configuration.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:51.510
Read basement, sedimentary cover, old sutures, and younger structures together to

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.550
reconstruct the events hidden beneath a relatively quiet surface.
